  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Network Transport:\n      - Removed all legacy overloads across transport, protocol, client, server, and session layers.\n      - Core API is now fully span-based (ReadOnlySpan<char> / ReadOnlySpan<byte>) for zero-copy performance.\n      - Transport layer retains Buffer-based APIs to preserve ownership control, pooling efficiency, and high-throughput batching.\n\n      WebSocket:\n      - Unified send pipeline: all WebSocket operations now use span-based input; no string/byte[] overloads remain.\n      - Simplified frame builder and removed redundant helpers, making the protocol layer smaller and easier to maintain.\n      - Improved consistency between client, server, and session protocols with a single clean API surface.\n\n      Core Cleanup:\n      - Removed duplicated code paths and overload noise, significantly reducing maintenance cost.\n      - Clarified ownership model: sync send manages its own buffers; async send transfers ownership to the send loop.\n      - Improved internal structure to support future optimizations and protocol extensions.\n\n      Performance:\n      - Reduced allocations across all network paths by eliminating implicit conversions and redundant buffer creation.\n      - More predictable memory behavior thanks to strict Buffer usage at the transport layer.\n      - Cleaner hot paths and better inlining opportunities for JIT.",
